        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f23f7faf-6e05-58b1-baed-2adca497599b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Little Missouri River, Missouri River, Devils Tower, Bear Lodge Mountains, Black Hills, Belle Fourche River, Three V Crossing, Marmarth, Crook County, Wyoming, Montana, South Dakota, North Dakota\n- Concepts: tributaries, river length, buttes, laccolithic landforms\n\nFacts:\n- The Little Missouri River is a 560-mile (901 km) tributary of the Missouri River in the northern Great Plains of the United States.\n- The Little Missouri River rises in western Crook County in northeastern Wyoming about 15 miles (24 km) west of Devils Tower.\n- The Little Missouri River flows northeast across a corner of southeastern Montana and into South Dakota.\n- Devils Tower, also called Bear Lodge Butte, is a laccolithic butte of igneous rock in the Bear Lodge Mountains, part of the Black Hills, in Crook County, northeastern Wyoming, above the Belle Fourche River.\n- Devils Tower rises 1,267 feet (386 m) above the Belle Fourche River and stands 867 feet (265 m) from base to summit.\n- Three V Crossing is on the Little Missouri River 19.1 miles north-northeast of Marmarth in North Dakota.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
